19:04.602 --> 19:07.563
DON: Well,
thanks, man.

19:07.647 --> 19:08.856
TEDDY: I knew
you could do it.

19:08.939 --> 19:11.859
Sure enough,
fucking crushed it.

19:18.616 --> 19:19.742
Incredible.

19:20.409 --> 19:21.452
DON: What is?

19:22.203 --> 19:23.996
TEDDY:
Just the detail.

19:24.914 --> 19:26.457
The best I've seen.

19:26.540 --> 19:29.502
DON: Uh, how can you
tell she's an alien?

19:29.585 --> 19:32.588
TEDDY: Well, the
signs are obvious.

19:33.964 --> 19:36.175
They did a hell of a job
on it, but the tells are there.

19:36.926 --> 19:38.344
Narrow feet.

19:38.427 --> 19:40.262
Thin cuticles.

19:41.389 --> 19:43.933
Slight overbite.

19:47.269 --> 19:49.355
Semi-obtruding
earlobes.

19:50.272 --> 19:51.315
See?

19:51.399 --> 19:52.983
High hair density.

19:53.901 --> 19:56.862
You won't notice unless you
know what you're looking for.

19:58.197 --> 20:00.157
DON: I guess
I can see it.

20:00.241 --> 20:04.328
It's like, if you don't
cook steaks a lot,

20:04.912 --> 20:06.664
you won't know when
it's cooked medium-rare.

20:06.747 --> 20:10.376
But if you cook steaks
all the time, you just know.

20:11.293 --> 20:15.256
You don't even have to
cut into it. You just... know.

20:18.300 --> 20:19.760
Hey. Hey, um...
(STAMMERS)

20:20.928 --> 20:22.680
Why are we
doing this?

20:23.222 --> 20:24.682
Is she itchy?

20:24.765 --> 20:26.976
No,Don
It's not itchy.

20:27.768 --> 20:30.271
Its genetic structure
is the same as ours,

20:31.147 --> 20:34.024
uh, but its nervous
system is different.

20:34.108 --> 20:37.486
The antihistamine reacts to the
neurotransmitters in its nervous system

20:37.570 --> 20:38.571
and weakens it.

20:40.281 --> 20:42.158
We're just leveling
the playing field.

20:43.117 --> 20:45.661
It's not torture. Torture
is what it's done to us.

20:46.579 --> 20:47.913
Huh.

20:48.956 --> 20:51.041
TEDDY: The sedative
should wear off soon.

20:51.125 --> 20:53.711
Should we go get dressed?
DON: Okay.

20:53.794 --> 20:55.004
TEDDY: Okay, come on.

20:55.087 --> 20:56.839
(FOOTSTEPS ASCENDING STAIRS)

21:08.893 --> 21:10.019
Is it too
tight?

21:10.102 --> 21:11.103
No, man.

21:12.813 --> 21:14.315
No, this was
my dad's shit.

21:14.940 --> 21:17.318
He left it behind
for a reason,

21:18.027 --> 21:19.612
so that it could be
put to good use.

21:20.654 --> 21:22.531
Everything's for
a reason, Don.

21:24.241 --> 21:25.576
It's too tight.

21:26.202 --> 21:27.244
I look stupid.

21:27.328 --> 21:28.412
No,
you don't.

21:28.496 --> 21:30.372
You look fine, honestly.
You look fine.

21:31.040 --> 21:33.626
Anyway... (CHUCKLES)
...what's that swine gonna do,

21:33.709 --> 21:36.420
call the fashion police
and arrest you?

21:36.504 --> 21:39.256
This isn't
abouthen

21:39.340 --> 21:41.050
Hey. (SIGHS)

21:41.133 --> 21:44.220
It is not
in control anymore.

21:44.303 --> 21:45.471
We are.

21:47.097 --> 21:49.809
Besides, I'll be doing
most of the talking anyway.

21:50.601 --> 21:53.854
In fact, maybe don't
say much. (GRUNTS)

21:53.938 --> 21:55.773
Like, you don't really
have to say much.

21:55.856 --> 21:56.857
Okay.

21:57.691 --> 21:59.568
Like, don't talk
at all, maybe.

22:00.861 --> 22:02.279
Oh.

22:02.363 --> 22:04.240
(GATE CREAKING OPEN)

22:09.286 --> 22:11.539
(GATE CREAKING SHUT)

22:15.751 --> 22:17.920
(LIGHT CLINKING)
(DOOR CLOSES)

22:20.923 --> 22:23.300
(FOOTSTEPS DESCENDING STAIRS)

22:23.384 --> 22:25.177
(EARS RINGING)

22:26.345 --> 22:27.721
TEDDY: Welcome.

22:29.890 --> 22:31.225
Are you conscious?

22:32.101 --> 22:33.310
What?
TEDDY: Is she conscious?

22:34.937 --> 22:35.980
(HESITATES)
I can only proceed

22:36.063 --> 22:37.857
if you're fully
conscious, so...

22:38.774 --> 22:40.317
Uh...

22:40.401 --> 22:41.819
What?

22:41.902 --> 22:43.487
TEDDY: Yes. Greetings.

22:43.571 --> 22:45.030
This is my home.

22:46.824 --> 22:47.908
Where...

22:51.787 --> 22:54.415
Is this...
Is this a hospital?

22:54.498 --> 22:57.001
TEDDY: No, this is
not a hospital. Is this...

22:58.294 --> 22:59.837
TEDDY: Fuck it.
I'm just gonna start.

22:59.920 --> 23:01.297
(CLEARS TH ROAT)

23:01.380 --> 23:04.341
"Welcome to the headquarters
of the human resistance.

23:04.425 --> 23:06.343
"Despite our
general suspicion

23:06.427 --> 23:09.221
"and disavowal of all
extant governing bodies,

23:09.305 --> 23:11.724
"and despite the fact that
you, as an Andromedan,

23:11.807 --> 23:13.809
"are not subject to the
human rights guidelines

23:13.893 --> 23:15.895
"detailed in the
Geneva Conventions,

23:15.978 --> 23:18.022
"we nevertheless endeavor
to adhere to those guidelines

23:18.105 --> 23:20.232
out of the humanist principles
to which they aspire."

23:21.734 --> 23:22.818
MICHELLE:
What is happening?

23:22.902 --> 23:26.155
I'm explaining to you that I
would like to keep all of this

23:26.238 --> 23:30.034
very above-board
and civilized. So...

23:30.117 --> 23:31.619
Where's
my hair?

23:31.702 --> 23:32.912
TEDDY: Your hair's
been destroyed.

23:33.537 --> 23:36.707
You shaved off my hair? TEDDY:
Yes, we've shaved off your hair.

23:36.790 --> 23:39.209
Why have you
shaved off my hair?

23:39.293 --> 23:41.712
To prevent you from
contacting your ship.

23:43.255 --> 23:44.381
My ship?

23:44.465 --> 23:45.507
TEDDY: Your ship.

23:46.508 --> 23:47.551
What ship?

23:49.595 --> 23:50.763
Your mother ship.

23:53.140 --> 23:54.433
Okay.

23:54.516 --> 23:55.768
Full disclosure:

23:55.851 --> 23:58.270
I've also applied a thin layer
of antihistamine cream

23:58.354 --> 23:59.605
to your skin...
MICHELLE: Excuse me.

23:59.688 --> 24:00.648
...which we'll need

24:00.773 --> 24:02.232
to reapply every day...
MICHELLE: Listen to me.

24:02.316 --> 24:04.193
...for full effectiveness.
Listen to me.

24:06.195 --> 24:07.237
I'm listening.

24:08.030 --> 24:09.031
MICHELLE; Right.

24:10.658 --> 24:12.284
Here's what's
gonna happen.

24:13.369 --> 24:15.955
And I wanna be clear,
I'm not threatening you.

24:16.914 --> 24:18.123
Or you.

24:18.749 --> 24:21.335
But the following
is my best guess

24:21.418 --> 24:24.254
of how the next 48 hours
are likely to transpire.

24:25.381 --> 24:26.966
The police,
and soon thereafter,

24:27.049 --> 24:28.634
the FBI, will begin
a statewide manhunt

24:28.717 --> 24:30.803
using all of the methods
at their disposal,

24:30.886 --> 24:34.598
and the combined resources
of neighboring jurisdictions.

24:34.682 --> 24:38.352
My company
is a key job creator

24:38.435 --> 24:40.479
and economic engine
of the region.

24:40.562 --> 24:41.689
I am crucial.

24:41.772 --> 24:45.609
Think of it like you've abducted
the governor, but worse.

24:46.443 --> 24:49.029
That's the level of bureaucratic
urgency you're contending with here.

24:49.113 --> 24:51.281
In all humility,
I can say that.

24:51.907 --> 24:54.535
I'm also a high-profile
female corporate executive.

24:54.618 --> 24:55.869
Does that
add a certain,

24:55.953 --> 24:57.454
you know, politicized
optics to this?

24:57.538 --> 24:58.831
I would say absolutely.

24:58.914 --> 25:02.209
I would say that's a tremendous
factor for you to consider here.

25:03.127 --> 25:05.170
Now, I don't make the rules,
and I don't enforce anything,

25:05.254 --> 25:10.134
and I am not in charge of the
situation in this room. You are.

25:10.217 --> 25:12.219
But you are
not in charge

25:12.302 --> 25:13.595
of what is happening
out there.

25:13.679 --> 25:15.222
And what is
happening out there

25:15.305 --> 25:17.182
is a rapid
cross-coordination

25:17.266 --> 25:18.976
of law enforcement
and digital media,

25:19.059 --> 25:21.687
which is all leading quite
inevitably to your imprisonment...

25:22.521 --> 25:23.647
and very
likely worse,

25:24.815 --> 25:26.025
if I can
be frank.

25:28.444 --> 25:32.072
I'm not privy to what their methods
might be under extreme duress,

25:32.156 --> 25:34.158
or yours,
for that matter.

25:34.241 --> 25:35.826
Butlcan
assure you

25:35.909 --> 25:38.287
that there is no
possible scenario

25:38.370 --> 25:39.872
where you benefit
from this incident,

25:39.955 --> 25:42.958
unless you cooperate
with me right now

25:43.042 --> 25:44.543
and negotiate
a deal that's fair

25:44.626 --> 25:46.003
and advantageous
to us both.

25:49.840 --> 25:52.593
(CHUCKLING)

25:53.844 --> 25:54.845
Okay.

25:54.928 --> 25:56.180
(CHUCKLES)

25:57.473 --> 25:58.807
Wow.
(CLICKS TONGUE)

26:00.476 --> 26:01.518
That was
really good.

26:02.478 --> 26:03.604
That was
really good.

26:05.147 --> 26:07.733
My pulse is racing right now.
Um... (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

26:09.359 --> 26:10.360
Fuck. (SIGHS)

26:10.444 --> 26:13.238
You got a real human
response out of me there,

26:13.322 --> 26:16.492
which is impressive given
your cellular composition and all.

26:16.575 --> 26:17.701
(HESITATES)
It's the truth.

26:17.785 --> 26:18.911
TEDDY: Well, no.
It's not the truth.

26:18.994 --> 26:20.454
Nothing you
say is true.

26:20.537 --> 26:24.917
Objective human truth has no
value in Andromedan cognition.

26:26.126 --> 26:28.629
Let's just unpack
the problem here.

26:28.712 --> 26:30.589
TEDDY: "Unpack"?
Wow, heady shit.

26:30.672 --> 26:33.467
Sure, let's unpack the
old fact bag, shall we?

26:33.550 --> 26:39.431
You are a high-ranking official
in the royal Andromedan court.

26:39.515 --> 26:43.644
And you've aided your species
in the techno-enslavement

26:43.727 --> 26:47.606
and the agro-corporate
disintegration of planet Earth, okay?

26:47.689 --> 26:50.776
And we need you to
bring us to your mother ship

26:50.859 --> 26:52.903
on the night of
the lunar eclipse

26:52.986 --> 26:55.823
to broker a sit-down
with your royal superiors.

26:55.906 --> 26:58.742
How's that? Fucking
unpacked enough for ya?

26:58.826 --> 27:01.120
I hear where you're
coming from. I do.

27:02.037 --> 27:04.039
And I respectfully
disagree.

27:04.706 --> 27:05.707
On which part?

27:07.751 --> 27:09.711
Primarily, I am
not an alien.

27:09.795 --> 27:12.548
You are. I've done thermal
imaging on your face.

27:12.631 --> 27:14.925
There's Andromedan code
all over your Instagram.

27:15.008 --> 27:16.552
You're barely
even hiding it.

27:18.303 --> 27:19.596
I mean,
look at you.

27:19.680 --> 27:23.142
I'm supposed to believe
you're a 45-year-old woman?

27:24.268 --> 27:25.561
Human woman?

27:25.644 --> 27:28.564
I mean, I follow a very
strict reverse-aging diet

27:28.647 --> 27:29.731
and therapy
program.

27:29.815 --> 27:32.818
It's very expensive, as you can
imagine, but I am not an alien.

27:33.819 --> 27:36.655
Well, there's really no
time for this. You are.

27:36.738 --> 27:37.739
I'm not.

27:42.077 --> 27:43.078
(SIGHS)

27:43.704 --> 27:44.830
All right, then.

27:45.455 --> 27:47.583
We're going to
give you the night

27:48.876 --> 27:50.127
to give your
statement.

27:50.961 --> 27:52.045
MICHELLE: My statement?

27:52.129 --> 27:53.505
TEDDY: That you will give
to your emperor...

27:54.089 --> 27:55.090
Uh-huh.

27:55.174 --> 27:56.633
...to grant us
passage to your ship

27:56.717 --> 28:00.304
and negotiate your species'
withdrawal from planet Earth.

28:00.387 --> 28:03.015
MICHELLE: Right. Could we
have a dialogue about this, please?

28:03.098 --> 28:06.602
Because what you're asking
me to do is not quite clear to me.

28:06.685 --> 28:07.978
TEDDY: I think
it is.

28:08.061 --> 28:10.772
And I want
you to know...

28:12.900 --> 28:14.902
this is really difficult
for me as well.

28:16.653 --> 28:17.988
You killed my family.

28:18.780 --> 28:21.283
You killed my community.
You killed my coworkers.

28:21.366 --> 28:22.534
You killed
the bees.

28:23.410 --> 28:24.661
So, given that,

28:25.871 --> 28:27.664
you should
really appreciate

28:27.748 --> 28:30.834
how super professional I'm
being right now by not gutting you.

28:32.085 --> 28:34.046
(INTENSE MUSIC)

28:42.679 --> 28:43.764
So,

28:43.847 --> 28:46.808
your sustenance
and waste disposal

28:46.892 --> 28:48.310
will be attended to
in the morning.

28:49.394 --> 28:51.355
I haven't gathered
adequate data

28:51.438 --> 28:54.358
on what type of sleep
you require, if any,

28:54.441 --> 28:56.360
but you should try
and get some, okay?

29:00.405 --> 29:02.074
I'm very sorry.

29:02.157 --> 29:05.827
I think that we maybe
got off on the wrong foot.

29:06.787 --> 29:10.082
And I would love to keep the
conversation going, please.

29:11.583 --> 29:13.585
Excuse me,
please?

29:14.336 --> 29:16.255
TEDDY: Don. Don.
Don, come on.

29:16.338 --> 29:18.048
MICHELLE: Come on,
let's keep talking.

29:19.549 --> 29:20.592
Please?

29:23.303 --> 29:24.304
Please?

29:33.146 --> 29:34.940
(DON CHUCKLING SOFTLY)

29:38.819 --> 29:39.820
TEDDY: Yeah!

29:39.903 --> 29:40.946
DON: Yeah.

29:41.488 --> 29:42.489
Don.

29:42.572 --> 29:44.449
Don, Don,
Don, Don!

29:44.533 --> 29:45.534
Don.

29:47.077 --> 29:48.245
(BOTH LAUGHING)

29:59.631 --> 30:02.801
(MICHELLE CRYING)

30:08.223 --> 30:10.142
(SIGHS DEEPLY)

30:14.938 --> 30:15.939
Hey.

30:16.898 --> 30:22.029
We can't see it as a
human woman, you know?

30:23.280 --> 30:26.241
It's not a person
named Michelle Fuller.

30:26.325 --> 30:28.994
It's the Fuller Humanoid.
That's all it is.

30:30.037 --> 30:34.666
Even if it was human,
and it's not, it's still evil.

30:34.750 --> 30:37.044
Pure,
corporate evil.

30:38.045 --> 30:40.172
It's killing
our planet, cuzzie.

30:40.672 --> 30:44.634
It was the lead executive on the
neonicotinoid linked to honeybee death.

30:44.718 --> 30:46.345
It only knows cruelty.

30:49.222 --> 30:51.308
Is it an alien?

30:52.684 --> 30:53.769
Yes.

30:59.733 --> 31:01.693
It knows you're
watching right now too.

31:03.070 --> 31:04.446
It's trying to gain
your sympathy.

31:04.529 --> 31:06.156
That shitty way that
you feel right now,

31:06.239 --> 31:07.491
that's how it
wants you to feel.

31:07.574 --> 31:10.494
It's mastered the art
of emotional manipulation.

31:11.203 --> 31:12.454
I'm sorry.

31:13.372 --> 31:17.376
I... I promise I won't
mess this up, Teddy.

31:17.459 --> 31:19.169
Don't apologize,
remember?

31:20.670 --> 31:22.547
We just stick
to the plan.

31:23.423 --> 31:26.343
We have four days
until the lunar eclipse,

31:26.426 --> 31:29.679
when the Andromedan ship
can return undetected. Yeah?

31:30.263 --> 31:31.390
Yeah.

31:31.473 --> 31:34.393
So, we need
the Fuller Humanoid

31:34.476 --> 31:36.478
to help us
make contact,

31:36.561 --> 31:39.481
so we can fight
for our self-worth.

31:40.607 --> 31:42.776
For our material
existence, Don.

31:43.652 --> 31:48.615
You know, lwish I could fix
everything that's been done to you.

31:50.784 --> 31:52.911
This is not
about me, Don.

31:54.579 --> 31:56.248
This is about everyone.

31:57.833 --> 32:01.503
And one day,
very soon, you'll see.

32:03.463 --> 32:07.008
And the world will see
you as you truly are.

32:07.676 --> 32:09.094
A hero.

32:09.678 --> 32:12.889
That's why
we stick to...

32:13.723 --> 32:16.268
We stick to...

32:17.018 --> 32:18.895
the plan.
Plan.

32:21.022 --> 32:22.607
See? You're
listening.

32:23.942 --> 32:24.943
Yeah.

32:39.332 --> 32:40.709
(MICHELLE SNIFFLES)

32:55.015 --> 32:56.016
(INTENSE MUSIC)

32:59.352 --> 33:01.980
WOMAN: I don't even
fucking know what's in it.

33:02.063 --> 33:04.774
I just eat the poison
they give me.

33:04.858 --> 33:05.942
But I know...

33:07.611 --> 33:09.696
they hide shit
in there

33:10.572 --> 33:13.825
to program
my cells,

33:15.076 --> 33:16.119
my blood.

33:17.829 --> 33:19.664
I see what
their plan is, okay?

33:21.082 --> 33:23.835
They sell me the sickness,
then they sell me the cure,

33:23.919 --> 33:26.755
and it's money
on both sides

33:26.838 --> 33:28.924
from the mind control...

33:29.007 --> 33:30.008
Um...

33:31.092 --> 33:33.345
industry, okay?

33:34.304 --> 33:35.305
Get it?

33:36.348 --> 33:38.099
But I'll do
it for you.

33:40.143 --> 33:41.561
You know, if it helps.

33:43.730 --> 33:45.148
If it makes me
not like me.

33:46.191 --> 33:49.694
Like I am, you know?
Like, weak.

33:50.612 --> 33:54.282
Your slob, cunt mom
will do it for you, baby.

33:56.034 --> 33:57.827
Just don't let them
get you too.

33:58.662 --> 33:59.788
(GIGGLES)

34:36.241 --> 34:38.159
TEDDY: You can go faster.
This isn't the spa.

34:38.243 --> 34:39.244
Okay.

34:49.838 --> 34:51.965
WOMAN: (OVER HEADPHONES)
With scientific evidence

34:52.048 --> 34:53.925
pointing to the potential
of other life

34:54.009 --> 34:57.971
even on our own planet
that we can't comprehend yet,

34:58.054 --> 35:00.098
and with unexplainable
phenomenon

35:00.181 --> 35:02.934
experienced by people
daily in the skies,

35:03.018 --> 35:06.187
in the oceans, and even
in their own backyard,

35:06.271 --> 35:08.690
I think it's kind of
just a little uninformed

35:08.773 --> 35:11.192
to not at least
acknowledge the potential

35:11.276 --> 35:15.196
that humankind may not be
the only intelligent life

35:15.280 --> 35:17.032
to ever exist
throughout the galaxy.

35:17.115 --> 35:20.327
(SYMPHONIC MUSIC BUILDING)

35:32.422 --> 35:35.634
MAN: (OVER HEADPHONES) But I
believe that there are definitely other

35:35.717 --> 35:36.926
higher intelligent
beings somewhere.

35:37.010 --> 35:39.929
I don't know if they're coming,
like I said, through the vibrations,

35:40.013 --> 35:42.057
coming through
frequencies into our world...

35:42.140 --> 35:43.183
(POLICE SIREN WAILS)

35:43.266 --> 35:45.935
...or if they're coming through
trillions and billions of miles of space,

35:46.019 --> 35:49.064
which seems kind of ridiculous
when you think about it, but...

35:49.147 --> 35:50.649
There's a whole--
WOMAN: But what if it's--

35:50.732 --> 35:52.776
What if it's both
of those things?

35:52.859 --> 35:53.943
What if it's not
one or the other?

35:54.027 --> 35:55.737
MAN: It could be a mixture
of everything. WOMAN: Yeah.

36:00.533 --> 36:01.534
TEDDY: Hey.

36:02.494 --> 36:03.995
Saw you there.
You all right?

36:05.246 --> 36:06.498
Uh, yeah.
I'm fine.

36:07.707 --> 36:08.792
How are you?

36:08.875 --> 36:09.876
(CHUCKLES)
I'm good.

36:10.460 --> 36:12.170
Off to work,
then, or...

36:13.129 --> 36:14.255
Uh-huh.

36:15.674 --> 36:18.259
I'm sorry, man. I know you're
like, "This fucking guy," right?

36:18.343 --> 36:19.344
TEDDY: No, no.

36:19.427 --> 36:22.055
No, it's all right.
It's just... You know...

36:22.138 --> 36:25.016
we haven't had a chance to catch
up in a while, 'cause, you know...

36:26.142 --> 36:28.770
all the shit,
and, uh... yeah.

36:28.853 --> 36:30.939
Just wanted to
check up on you.

36:31.564 --> 36:32.857
Casey, I'm good.
What's up?

36:32.941 --> 36:35.110
Nothing's up, man.
I just...

36:35.193 --> 36:38.655
I know I wasn't always the best
babysitter back in the day, but, um...

36:38.738 --> 36:40.740
I do want you
to be okay.

36:43.993 --> 36:45.578
You still up
there with Don?

36:46.538 --> 36:47.539
Yep.

36:47.622 --> 36:48.873
Great. Well...

36:49.833 --> 36:51.042
I think about
you sometimes.

36:51.126 --> 36:54.170
Not... Not in a weird
way, just... Yeah.

36:55.797 --> 36:57.340
I'm a different guy
now. I've grown up.

36:57.424 --> 36:59.300
So, if you ever need
help with anything, just...

37:00.927 --> 37:02.387
I'm good.

37:03.263 --> 37:05.140
I just gotta
get to work. So...

37:05.223 --> 37:06.725
Maybe I'll stop
by sometime.

37:06.808 --> 37:10.729
Yeah, I mean... I'm...
I'm super busy right now.

37:11.604 --> 37:13.022
Crazy busy.
Right.

37:13.106 --> 37:15.984
But... Yeah, maybe
sometime later.

37:16.067 --> 37:18.236
Later, yeah.
All right.

37:18.945 --> 37:20.155
Cool. See ya.

37:21.489 --> 37:23.283
Take it
easy.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.701
See ya,
Teddy.

37:26.327 --> 37:28.288
MAN: (OVER HEADPHONES)
Some people say they're all demons.

37:28.371 --> 37:31.708
A lot of people think they're
higher-intelligent beings

37:31.791 --> 37:34.627
from a different
wavelength.

37:35.336 --> 37:37.714
That's a possibility too, I
guess. I don't know anything.

37:37.797 --> 37:40.383
So I'm not saying, like,
one way or the other.

37:40.467 --> 37:42.177
I just, personally,
I have my opinion,

37:42.260 --> 37:43.928
and I think it's somehow
all connected.

37:44.012 --> 37:47.766
WOMAN: I think that
all of those things are

37:47.849 --> 37:50.602
each a small part
of one giant reality...

37:50.685 --> 37:52.729
Ewan! What's up, man?
EWAN: Morning.

37:52.812 --> 37:54.606
MAN: (OVER HEADPHONES)
I honestly start to believe

37:54.689 --> 37:56.191
that we're all in, like,
a simulation.

37:56.274 --> 37:58.067
And I don't wanna say
it's like The Matrix, but...

38:04.324 --> 38:05.950
TEDDY: What's
wrong, Tina?

38:06.034 --> 38:08.286
My frickin' hand
is still killing me.

38:08.369 --> 38:11.080
Christ. Did you file that
shit With OSHA yet?

38:11.164 --> 38:14.000
I looked into
it, but I--

38:14.751 --> 38:17.378
I don't think
it's a violation.

38:18.129 --> 38:23.092
Tina, their machinery cut you, and
you get punished for missing quotas?

38:23.176 --> 38:24.844
That's a...
That's a violation.

38:25.762 --> 38:27.430
Fucking demons.

38:29.307 --> 38:31.601
I just don't
want any trouble.

38:36.314 --> 38:39.567
Don't you worry. One day
soon, it's all gonna change.

38:39.651 --> 38:41.861
They're not going to get away
with this shit in the end, okay?

38:43.279 --> 38:44.906
I promise you that.

38:44.989 --> 38:49.577
On Monday afternoon, following what
coworkers describe as a routine workday,

38:49.661 --> 38:54.415
Auxolith Biomedical CEO
Michelle Fuller got into her car,

38:54.499 --> 38:58.545
passed the security gate at Auxolith
headquarters in Fayette County, Georgia,

38:58.628 --> 39:00.255
and drove
towards home.

39:00.338 --> 39:02.590
That was nearly
48 hours ago.

39:02.674 --> 39:04.843
No one has heard
from her since.

39:04.926 --> 39:07.512
Authorities now believe
there is a strong chance...

39:07.595 --> 39:08.596
Hey.

39:08.680 --> 39:12.308
Oh, yo. What up, Carlos? I brought
some fresh honey in, for toast.

39:12.392 --> 39:14.853
Oh, great. Thank
you, Teddy. Yeah.

39:14.936 --> 39:16.938
NEWS ANCHOR: A furious
statewide manhunt is now underway,

39:17.021 --> 39:19.357
with state police urging
Fayette County locals

39:19.440 --> 39:22.193
to come forward with
any information at all.

39:22.277 --> 39:24.779
Given Fuller's wealth
and high profile,

39:24.863 --> 39:27.282
state police are not
ruling out the possibility

39:27.365 --> 39:29.951
that Fuller is being
held for ransom,

39:30.034 --> 39:32.704
though, as of yet,
there is no evidence

39:32.787 --> 39:34.539
to suggest this
might be the case.

39:34.622 --> 39:37.208
The only clue
authorities have...

39:37.292 --> 39:40.128
(SYMPHONIC MUSIC PLAYS)

39:40.920 --> 39:42.213
(BEES BUZZING)

40:11.868 --> 40:13.578
TEDDY: Hey, cuz.
Did she eat?

40:14.537 --> 40:15.538
No.

40:15.622 --> 40:16.956
Bedpan?

40:17.040 --> 40:18.041
DON: No.

40:22.587 --> 40:25.506
Maybe she's
too scared to go?

40:25.590 --> 40:27.425
TEDDY: No, she's not
too scared to go.

40:28.176 --> 40:30.970
It's trying to
pity-trap our asses.

40:31.054 --> 40:32.639
It's a ploy.
(DOOR CREAKS OPEN)

40:32.722 --> 40:35.058
We're not gonna let
it pity-trap us, are we?

40:35.141 --> 40:36.684
(FOOTSTEPS
APPROACHING)

40:36.768 --> 40:38.269
DON: No.

40:38.853 --> 40:39.979
Just stay
over there.

40:40.063 --> 40:41.230
Okay, Teddy.

41:02.335 --> 41:05.922
MICHELLE: (OVER RECORDING)
Um, I am an alien from outer space.

41:06.005 --> 41:10.343
I live here on planet Earth,
but I am not a human being.

41:10.426 --> 41:13.638
My mother ship
is coming to Earth,

41:13.721 --> 41:17.475
and I would like to bring my
new friend with me. Thanks.

41:20.019 --> 41:22.605
Uh-huh. So...

41:23.940 --> 41:25.650
this is a
joke, then?

41:26.359 --> 41:30.488
You're trying to simulate
sapient humor, or...

41:30.571 --> 41:32.031
That was the
best I could do.

41:32.115 --> 41:33.282
TEDDY: This is the
best you could do?

41:33.366 --> 41:35.076
You didn't even say it
in your own language.

41:37.078 --> 41:38.955
Sorry. That was
the best I could do.

41:39.038 --> 41:40.957
No, it isn't.

41:42.709 --> 41:45.086
What would you
like me to say, then?

41:45.795 --> 41:48.172
Well, I already
did that. Um...

41:48.256 --> 41:52.510
I would like you to request
an audience with your emperor

41:52.593 --> 41:56.180
to discuss the terms of your
species' withdrawal from Earth.

41:56.305 --> 41:58.641
MICHELLE: And I did
that. But convincingly.

41:58.766 --> 42:01.019
Well, I think that's
gonna be difficult. Why?

42:02.645 --> 42:04.897
At the risk
of repeating myself,

42:04.981 --> 42:06.607
I'm not an alien.

42:08.151 --> 42:09.569
(CRASH)

42:13.906 --> 42:14.991
Teddy?

42:16.200 --> 42:17.452
What?

42:17.535 --> 42:21.497
I thought all night
about our situation here,

42:21.581 --> 42:23.291
and I think I know
what's going on.

42:23.958 --> 42:26.085
Okay. Yeah,
please, enlighten me.

42:26.169 --> 42:31.049
So, look, if eel qualified here
because I am a chemist by training,

42:31.132 --> 42:33.051
but I also have
a psych degree.

42:33.134 --> 42:34.510
Oh. Okay.
Wow. Great.

42:35.178 --> 42:36.596
A degree from
a university?

42:36.679 --> 42:39.307
From a credentialist scam for
laundering privilege? Amazing.

42:39.390 --> 42:41.267
Well, yeah,
I do have a degree.

42:41.350 --> 42:43.686
And I also have read
a lot about this.

42:43.770 --> 42:46.731
You can't talk your way
out of this again.

42:47.482 --> 42:49.400
I'm not a
kid anymore.

42:49.484 --> 42:50.735
(GULPS)

42:52.612 --> 42:56.240
I think you're in
a kind of echo chamber.

42:56.324 --> 42:57.658
Echo chamber?
Right now?

42:57.742 --> 42:59.368
Mm-hmm.
Echo?

43:01.537 --> 43:04.916
Yeah, I read the same 5,000
think pieces about that too.

43:04.999 --> 43:08.377
You're consuming
content on the Internet

43:08.461 --> 43:12.381
that is reinforcing
this sort of warped,

43:12.465 --> 43:15.009
subjective idea
of reality.

43:15.093 --> 43:16.511
This is your
best shot at me?

43:17.095 --> 43:19.639
Some "rabbit holes" bullshit
you read in the Times?

43:19.722 --> 43:21.099
Come on.
Come on.

43:21.182 --> 43:23.017
Can we have
a dialogue, please?

43:23.101 --> 43:24.727
Don't call it
a dialogue.

43:24.811 --> 43:26.270
This isn't
Death of a Salesman.

43:26.354 --> 43:28.231
Okay, can we
talk, please?

43:28.314 --> 43:29.732
Or are you just gonna
keep doing this?

43:29.816 --> 43:31.317
Okay. We don't need to talk.

43:31.400 --> 43:33.444
Because I know exactly
what you're going to say.

43:33.528 --> 43:36.030
You're going to say that
I'm in some kind of

43:36.114 --> 43:40.368
Internet-induced auto-hypnotic
feedback loop,

43:40.451 --> 43:42.662
and gatekeepers
and norms,

43:42.745 --> 43:44.247
and all that weak
hegemonic horseshit.

43:44.330 --> 43:47.166
But that is precisely
the limp-dick rhetoric

43:47.250 --> 43:48.501
that you've been
instructed

43:48.584 --> 43:50.294
to counter the
human insurgency with.

43:50.378 --> 43:53.089
That's the fucking
hyper-normalized dialectic

43:53.172 --> 43:55.633
by which you've convinced
seven and a half billion people

43:55.716 --> 43:57.135
that they're not
your captives.

43:57.718 --> 44:02.223
To keep us believing in
these fucking false institutional,

44:02.306 --> 44:04.600
fucking shybboleths.

44:05.476 --> 44:07.270
You mean,
"shibboleths."

44:07.353 --> 44:08.896
That's what
I said.

44:08.980 --> 44:10.022
You said...

44:10.106 --> 44:11.190
Yeah,
whatever.

44:11.274 --> 44:14.902
Sorry. I guess grammar is a
false Andromedan construct as well.

44:20.116 --> 44:21.284
(GRUNTS)

44:22.869 --> 44:24.453
Fucking...

44:24.537 --> 44:26.831
(BANGING)

44:27.832 --> 44:29.333
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

44:34.338 --> 44:35.423
I'm sorry.

44:37.175 --> 44:38.467
You're angry.

44:38.551 --> 44:39.927
I see that.

44:40.720 --> 44:42.889
I even think you have
a right to be angry.

44:42.972 --> 44:44.098
You do?

44:44.182 --> 44:47.351
Yes! But we need
to have an honest talk

44:47.435 --> 44:48.811
in good faith

44:48.895 --> 44:50.813
about what is
going on here.

44:50.897 --> 44:52.648
TEDDY: Yes. You're
right. Let's talk it out.

44:52.732 --> 44:53.816
Let's create
a safe space,

44:53.900 --> 44:56.694
safe words,
good faith, dialogue.

44:56.777 --> 44:59.197
When you talk about this,
when you talk about that,

44:59.280 --> 45:00.948
and what we talk about
when we talk about

45:01.032 --> 45:03.451
fucking talk, talk, talk,
talk, talk, talk, talk,

45:03.534 --> 45:06.037
talking forever until
we're all fucking dead!

45:06.120 --> 45:07.246
Yeah, I agree.

45:07.330 --> 45:09.749
So, what is this exactly
that you want?

45:10.791 --> 45:13.169
Like, what do you
really want? Is it money?

45:14.670 --> 45:16.672
Your capital
has no value to us.

45:17.506 --> 45:19.550
So, what is it, then?
A power thing?

45:19.634 --> 45:20.718
A sex thing?

45:23.346 --> 45:25.556
We have no interest
in you, sexually.

45:26.349 --> 45:27.683
Irrespective
of the fact

45:27.767 --> 45:30.394
that your
reproductive organs

45:30.478 --> 45:32.104
may not be compatible
with ours,

45:32.188 --> 45:34.565
my cousin and I have also
been chemically castrated.

45:36.734 --> 45:38.569
Oh, Jesus Christ.
Okay.

45:38.653 --> 45:41.322
But I figured you might try
to lure us in that way.

45:41.405 --> 45:43.032
Hence the precaution.
See, Don?

45:48.579 --> 45:50.915
Don. Teddy.

45:52.208 --> 45:53.417
Come on.

45:53.501 --> 45:54.961
We have options here.

45:55.044 --> 45:56.712
We do.
No.

45:56.796 --> 45:57.838
There are
no options.

45:58.589 --> 46:00.174
There are no rules.

46:00.675 --> 46:03.594
There are no deals.
There's no payoff.

46:03.678 --> 46:05.012
There's no money.

46:05.096 --> 46:08.099
There is no legal system.

46:08.182 --> 46:09.267
There's no Congress.

46:09.350 --> 46:11.143
There is no America.

46:11.227 --> 46:14.855
There's no global
democratic order, okay?

46:14.939 --> 46:16.857
So, don't talk to me like
I'm a dipshit,

46:16.941 --> 46:18.442
because I'm
not a dipshit.

46:18.526 --> 46:20.361
I'm a guy that knows
what the fuck is happening,

46:20.444 --> 46:22.154
and you will
not defeat me,

46:22.238 --> 46:24.365
you sick Andromedan fuck!

46:27.243 --> 46:28.661
Teddy, I'm sorry.

46:30.162 --> 46:31.330
You need help.

46:33.082 --> 46:34.375
You're mentally ill.

46:35.459 --> 46:36.460
(LOUD SLAP)

46:40.464 --> 46:41.465
(MICHELLE GROANING)

46:44.760 --> 46:46.804
Everybody denies
it at first,

46:47.888 --> 46:49.515
and then
they confess.

47:00.901 --> 47:02.695
(SYMPHONIC MUSIC SWELLS)

47:07.700 --> 47:10.661
TEDDY: Fucking...
Fucking fuck.

47:10.745 --> 47:13.873
Fucking lie. Fucking...

47:13.956 --> 47:16.751
Fuck! (SCREAMS)

47:19.628 --> 47:21.005
Fuck!

47:51.744 --> 47:54.372
(MUSIC CONCLUDES)

48:06.801 --> 48:09.720
TEDDY: I didn't discover them
on my own.

48:09.804 --> 48:12.223
I stand on the
shoulders of giants.

48:12.306 --> 48:17.978
The PA-99-N2 microlensing event
proved that there was an exoplanet.

48:18.062 --> 48:21.607
And Gideon55's YouTube studies
into Andromedan infiltration

48:21.690 --> 48:23.818
paved the way
for my own research.

48:23.901 --> 48:27.988
But I was the one who discovered
how to identify them, okay?

48:28.531 --> 48:30.741
I created that content.

48:30.825 --> 48:33.160
Obviously I've never been
on the ship before.

48:33.244 --> 48:36.205
But I know enough
to render it on my laptop.

48:36.288 --> 48:39.708
The journey there
will be instantaneous.

48:39.792 --> 48:43.170
But once we're on board,
inside their chemical atmosphere,

48:43.254 --> 48:44.797
they may be able to
hear our thoughts.

48:44.880 --> 48:50.052
So keep your mind clear and
decisive during the negotiations.

48:51.011 --> 48:52.721
They will see

48:52.805 --> 48:57.268
that we are men
of honor and dignity.

48:57.351 --> 49:01.105
And that Earth, with its vast
resources and human ingenuity,

49:01.689 --> 49:04.191
has much that
we can offer.

49:04.275 --> 49:10.906
So much more than this fucking
worthless death spiral into chaos and shit.

49:11.699 --> 49:14.201
And if they won't
listen to reason,

49:14.285 --> 49:16.829
well, I have a plan
for that, too.

49:19.623 --> 49:22.543
DON: What will our
lives be like in space?

49:24.753 --> 49:25.754
In space?

49:26.672 --> 49:29.008
Aren't we going
to live in space?

49:31.177 --> 49:32.553
Well, bud, uh...

49:34.054 --> 49:35.931
we'll only be gone
for a few hours.

49:36.015 --> 49:39.185
We're not leaving Earth
for good. We're saving it.

49:40.311 --> 49:42.521
So we have
to stay here?

49:43.230 --> 49:44.648
TEDDY: Well, yeah.
Of course.

49:45.524 --> 49:47.234
But we're saving it.

49:47.318 --> 49:50.196
So, it'll be a good
place to live again.

49:50.279 --> 49:53.073
So, everything
will be okay.

49:55.117 --> 49:57.495
Yeah. I know.

49:58.245 --> 49:59.705
Sorry.

49:59.788 --> 50:01.165
TEDDY: It's
okay, man.

50:07.379 --> 50:10.007
Ever since those
shots you gave me,

50:11.008 --> 50:13.219
I've felt weird.

50:13.302 --> 50:15.429
And crazy.

50:15.513 --> 50:17.765
And sometimes sad.

50:18.682 --> 50:20.643
Have you felt
that way too?

50:22.102 --> 50:25.105
It'll pass. Don't worry.

50:27.358 --> 50:28.776
It'll pass.

50:29.610 --> 50:30.653
Mmm.

50:49.421 --> 50:51.674
(CHAINS RATTLING)

50:52.883 --> 50:54.510
(MICHELLE GRUNTING)

51:02.643 --> 51:03.894
(MICHELLE PANTING)

51:07.273 --> 51:09.775
(GRUNTING CONTINUES)

51:13.737 --> 51:15.489
(DOOR CREAKS OPEN)

51:20.703 --> 51:23.205
(DOOR CREAKS SHUT)

51:26.500 --> 51:27.585
MICHELLE:
Good morning.

51:28.127 --> 51:29.420
TEDDY: You're
out of breath.

51:30.004 --> 51:31.880
MICHELLE:
Oh, yes. You...

51:33.132 --> 51:34.592
you make
me nervous.

51:38.762 --> 51:42.558
Um, so, I've... I've been
doing a lot of pondering.

51:42.641 --> 51:46.228
And I think we
should start over.

51:47.563 --> 51:48.939
I wanna
help you.

51:50.065 --> 51:51.525
And given that,

51:52.151 --> 51:55.321
there is something that I
should have said to you earlier

51:55.404 --> 51:58.449
that I am finally prepared
to say to you now.

51:59.199 --> 52:00.492
With conviction.

52:02.745 --> 52:04.455
I am an alien.

52:08.125 --> 52:09.251
I admit it.

52:11.003 --> 52:13.756
You were right all along.
I am an alien.

52:15.257 --> 52:19.178
I mean, you can't blame me for
trying to conceal it for as long as I did.

52:19.261 --> 52:23.057
Part of my mission here on Earth
is to blend in and so forth, so...

52:26.518 --> 52:27.686
Look, I'm very tired.

52:27.770 --> 52:29.730
And I know that
this doesn't...

52:30.939 --> 52:33.317
sound as forceful,

52:33.400 --> 52:37.446
or the verisimilitude is not what
you would want it to be necessarily,

52:37.529 --> 52:40.824
but I can assure you
I mean what I say.

52:40.908 --> 52:44.495
And I would like to move
forward now, to a solution.

52:48.123 --> 52:49.416
I'm an alien.

53:10.479 --> 53:12.147
You wanna start over?

53:13.649 --> 53:14.650
Yes.

53:16.151 --> 53:17.152
Good.

53:17.945 --> 53:19.613
Let's
start over.

53:20.614 --> 53:21.615
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

53:21.699 --> 53:22.825
TEDDY: I was hoping

53:23.867 --> 53:26.662
we could agree on your
genus and avoid a painful test,

53:26.745 --> 53:28.330
but you forced
my hand.

53:28.414 --> 53:30.749
(MUFFLED) I...
I admitted it. Okay?

53:31.500 --> 53:32.501
I admitted it.

53:32.584 --> 53:33.794
TEDDY: I'm sorry.

53:33.877 --> 53:37.047
I'm a humane person.
I do not want to do this.

53:38.465 --> 53:40.008
I'm an alien.

53:40.759 --> 53:42.803
I am an alien!
I am...

53:42.886 --> 53:44.054
TEDDY: I agree.

53:44.138 --> 53:46.223
("BASKET CASE"
BY GREEN DAY PLAYING)

53:46.306 --> 53:49.309
Do you have the time
to listen to me whine?

53:49.643 --> 53:54.148
About nothing
and everything all at once

53:55.983 --> 53:57.317
I am one of those...

53:57.401 --> 53:59.403
Uh, are you sure
it works?

54:00.654 --> 54:02.656
She already
admitted it.

54:02.740 --> 54:04.783
It killed our
family, cuzzie.

54:04.867 --> 54:06.076
DON: Yeah, but...

54:06.744 --> 54:08.912
this doesn't
seem right.

54:12.416 --> 54:14.585
Please stop.
Please, please.

54:14.668 --> 54:16.670
Don't. Don't.
Don't, don't.

54:16.754 --> 54:18.005
Don't do this.
Don't do this.

54:21.133 --> 54:23.177
Okay, here comes the first
wave. MICHELLE: No, no, no.

54:23.260 --> 54:25.095
Wait! Don't,
don't, don't, don't.

54:25.179 --> 54:27.848
(MICHELLE SCREAMING)

54:32.895 --> 54:34.313
Please don't.

54:34.396 --> 54:35.689
Trust me,
Don.

54:35.773 --> 54:36.940
Trust me!

54:37.024 --> 54:38.275
Second wave.

54:38.358 --> 54:40.444
(MICHELLE CONTINUES
SCREAMING)

54:47.868 --> 54:50.245
(MUSIC STARTS DISTORTING)

54:50.329 --> 54:52.956
(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)

54:54.291 --> 54:56.543
(MICHELLE CONTINUES
SCREAMING)

54:59.546 --> 55:00.923
DON: Teddy, no!

55:07.012 --> 55:08.347
(FAINT SCREAMING)

55:12.726 --> 55:14.770
You'll kill
her, Teddy!

55:16.980 --> 55:18.190
Can you stop?

55:18.273 --> 55:19.775
Teddy, stop!

55:19.858 --> 55:21.527
Donny, back up!

55:21.610 --> 55:22.903
I'm sorry.

55:25.906 --> 55:28.408
(MICHELLE CONTINUES SCREAMING)

55:36.375 --> 55:39.169
(SHORT-CIRCUITING)

55:42.005 --> 55:43.882
What the fuck?

55:44.758 --> 55:46.176
MICHELLE:
That's enough!

55:48.637 --> 55:50.514
What's wrong
with you, man?

55:51.849 --> 55:53.600
She could've
died.

55:53.684 --> 55:56.478
No. No, Don.
You don't understand.

55:56.562 --> 55:57.563
What?

55:59.439 --> 56:00.482
It was off
the charts.

56:01.191 --> 56:03.402
The output, it's never
reached that threshold before.

56:03.485 --> 56:04.653
DON:
"Before"?

56:04.736 --> 56:06.530
TEDDY: Could you get me
a towel, please?

56:28.176 --> 56:30.387
I wish to...
(CUTTING RESTRAINTS)

56:30.470 --> 56:32.264
...apologize profusely.

56:36.268 --> 56:38.395
I did not realize...

56:39.688 --> 56:41.023
Your Majesty.

56:41.106 --> 56:42.190
What?

56:42.274 --> 56:44.818
TEDDY: I stupidly
thought you were admin.

56:46.445 --> 56:47.738
I did
not realize,

56:49.114 --> 56:50.407
at that voltage...

56:51.617 --> 56:54.328
You have the
royal genetic code.

56:55.037 --> 56:56.038
I'm sorry.

56:56.705 --> 56:57.706
I didn't know.

56:58.874 --> 57:00.042
I didn't know.

57:05.422 --> 57:07.674
The most important thing I
want to stress to you right now

57:07.758 --> 57:11.011
is I never want to
put this behind us. Never.

57:12.679 --> 57:14.973
What happened is
part of all of us now.

57:15.057 --> 57:17.601
And it doesn't go away, and it
doesn't get swept under the rug,

57:17.684 --> 57:19.311
and it doesn't
get excused.

57:19.394 --> 57:20.771
Not on
my watch.

57:20.854 --> 57:22.731
This one sticks.
Forever.

57:23.357 --> 57:25.275
I am putting this up

57:25.359 --> 57:27.736
on the corporate
masthead for all to see.

57:27.819 --> 57:29.655
For everyone in
our company

57:29.738 --> 57:31.782
and our industry
to learn from.

57:32.783 --> 57:35.243
That's why I'm meeting all of
the victims' families this week,

57:35.327 --> 57:37.245
to let them know we
are going to do better.

57:38.121 --> 57:41.124
Maybe we don't even try to
market a product like this anymore.

57:41.208 --> 57:45.087
Or maybe... maybe we
take this experience to grow,

57:45.170 --> 57:47.130
and to get this
formula right.

57:47.214 --> 57:50.133
Because I really do think,
if clone correctly, and safely,

57:50.217 --> 57:54.012
this could be a product that
could help someone like your mom.

57:54.096 --> 57:56.598
But right now, we would
like to do what's right,

57:56.682 --> 57:58.934
and cover the expenses
for your mother's treatment,

57:59.017 --> 58:02.104
in hopes that her condition
might one day improve.

58:02.187 --> 58:04.064
We will not
tolerate the idea

58:04.147 --> 58:06.817
of you or your family bearing
the financial burden of this.

58:06.900 --> 58:09.361
We are covering
all of it.

58:09.444 --> 58:11.113
This one's on us.

58:11.196 --> 58:13.532
And, again,
we're just so sorry.

58:19.079 --> 58:23.208
(FAST-PACED MUSIC)

59:01.788 --> 59:03.248
You'll have to
excuse me.

59:03.331 --> 59:07.294
It's my best attempt
to approximate

59:07.377 --> 59:10.672
the royal treatment to
which you are accustomed.

59:11.715 --> 59:13.800
MICHELLE: Oh,
it's great. Thank you.

59:13.884 --> 59:15.677
There was a wig
in the bathroom.

59:15.761 --> 59:16.970
Did you want me to wear that?

59:17.054 --> 59:18.472
TEDDY: No, no.
It's just an option.

59:18.555 --> 59:19.556
MICHELLE; I'm fine.

59:19.639 --> 59:21.600
TEDDY: And I want to apologize

59:21.683 --> 59:24.603
for not approaching you
with proper courtesy.

59:24.686 --> 59:27.022
Not realizing, of course,
what you were.

59:27.105 --> 59:30.901
That you shared blood
with the emperor himself.

59:30.984 --> 59:32.402
MICHELLE: Oh, that's
perfectly all right.

59:32.486 --> 59:35.614
TEDDY: The truth is, we
will never make progress here

59:35.697 --> 59:38.575
if we can't speak
eyeball-to-eyeball,

59:38.658 --> 59:42.204
as the most evolved examples
of our respective species.

59:42.287 --> 59:43.288
MICHELLE: /agree.

59:43.371 --> 59:44.372
TEDDY: Good.
MICHELLE: Excellent.

59:44.456 --> 59:46.750
(THUDDING)

59:48.418 --> 59:51.922
TEDDY: Well,
on that note, enjoy.

01:00:01.807 --> 01:00:02.933
It's a lovely home.

01:00:05.060 --> 01:00:06.103
Thank you.

01:00:06.728 --> 01:00:07.729
Mmm.

01:00:08.438 --> 01:00:09.439
Just you here?

01:00:09.940 --> 01:00:10.941
Yes.

01:00:11.858 --> 01:00:12.859
MICHELLE; Always?

01:00:14.945 --> 01:00:16.113
Sorry?

01:00:16.196 --> 01:00:17.948
Has-- Has it always
just been you?

01:00:18.031 --> 01:00:19.407
Um, well...

01:00:20.867 --> 01:00:25.372
I'd prefer if we didn't delve
too deeply into the personal,

01:00:25.455 --> 01:00:26.498
if you don't mind.

01:00:26.581 --> 01:00:29.251
Mmm. Sure,
that's fine.

01:00:29.334 --> 01:00:30.335
Thank you.

01:00:34.840 --> 01:00:36.133
So, what...

01:00:36.216 --> 01:00:38.969
Why don't you tell me more
about your movement?

01:00:39.052 --> 01:00:40.595
My What?

01:00:40.679 --> 01:00:42.764
MICHELLE: Your movement.
What you're doing.

01:00:45.183 --> 01:00:48.937
Respectfully,
we are not a movement.

01:00:49.020 --> 01:00:50.188
Oh.

01:00:50.272 --> 01:00:52.983
A movement is made up
of many people.

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:54.734
I did this all
on my own.

01:00:55.819 --> 01:00:57.154
MICHELLE: Of course.

01:00:57.237 --> 01:00:59.906
With the help of my
colleague, of course.

01:00:59.990 --> 01:01:01.158
MICHELLE: Well,
it's very impressive.

01:01:01.241 --> 01:01:02.450
TEDDY: Thank you.
MICHELLE: I'm...

01:01:02.534 --> 01:01:05.412
I'm all for people
who can do that.

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:08.748
You know, the
activism thing.

01:01:11.877 --> 01:01:14.462
99.9% of what's
called activism

01:01:14.546 --> 01:01:16.965
is really
personal exhibitionism

01:01:17.048 --> 01:01:20.343
and brand maintenance
in disguise.

01:01:20.427 --> 01:01:22.387
Mmm. Okay.

01:01:23.054 --> 01:01:24.472
TEDDY: I used
to be the same way.

01:01:26.266 --> 01:01:29.519
I ran through the whole
digestive tract in...

01:01:30.353 --> 01:01:31.563
five years?

01:01:32.856 --> 01:01:36.818
Alt-right, alt-lite,
leftist, Marxist.

01:01:37.194 --> 01:01:39.321
All those
stupid badges.

01:01:39.404 --> 01:01:42.616
I went shopping hungry, and I
just bought the whole store.

01:01:42.699 --> 01:01:43.992
(CHUCKLES)

01:01:44.075 --> 01:01:45.076
Mmm-hmm.

01:01:46.203 --> 01:01:48.788
TEDDY: But I was just
looking in the wrong places.

01:01:48.872 --> 01:01:52.626
Until I discovered you.

01:01:52.709 --> 01:01:55.295
Well, again, it is
very impressive.

01:01:55.378 --> 01:01:57.547
Thank you.

01:01:59.424 --> 01:02:00.425
You as well, Don.

01:02:01.051 --> 01:02:02.177
TEDDY: You'll...
Um...

01:02:03.345 --> 01:02:04.512
You'll have to
excuse my colleague.

01:02:04.596 --> 01:02:06.640
He prefers not
to converse.

01:02:06.723 --> 01:02:08.934
Uh, can I go
to the bathroom?

01:02:09.017 --> 01:02:10.477
TEDDY: in just
a minute, Don.

01:02:11.478 --> 01:02:12.646
We're eating
right now.

01:02:18.318 --> 01:02:19.903
I see you're apiarists.

01:02:19.986 --> 01:02:21.446
TEDDY: Of sorts.

01:02:21.529 --> 01:02:22.906
MICHELLE: I've taken
an interest as well.

01:02:22.989 --> 01:02:25.200
TEDDY: Hmm.
So I've heard.

01:02:25.283 --> 01:02:27.244
MICHELLE: Magnificent
creatures, honeybees.

01:02:27.327 --> 01:02:28.662
Very much so.

01:02:29.246 --> 01:02:31.248
Earth's most
admirable creation.

01:02:32.123 --> 01:02:34.709
Well, shit, I've literally said
those exact words before.

01:02:40.715 --> 01:02:44.386
Right, so, um, what is it
that you admire about them?

01:02:47.055 --> 01:02:48.390
About bees? Uh...

01:02:50.433 --> 01:02:51.893
Complex society.

01:02:51.977 --> 01:02:53.103
Work ethic.

01:02:53.687 --> 01:02:55.313
They do their duty,
they build their worlds

01:02:55.397 --> 01:02:59.442
without complaint or piety
or self-obsession.

01:03:02.529 --> 01:03:03.613
Mm-hmm.

01:03:03.697 --> 01:03:04.698
All true.

01:03:07.784 --> 01:03:11.621
Which is why they're
so easy to exploit, right?

01:03:12.706 --> 01:03:14.666
I just admire their
resolve. That's all.

01:03:15.750 --> 01:03:17.168
Eveninthe
face of peril.

01:03:18.545 --> 01:03:19.546
Well, we can
agree on that.

01:03:26.136 --> 01:03:27.470
What sort of peril,
by the way?

01:03:28.388 --> 01:03:29.389
MICHELLE: Sorry?

01:03:29.472 --> 01:03:31.850
You said bees
have faced peril.

01:03:31.933 --> 01:03:33.310
Such as?

01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.313
Uh, what do you
want me to say?

01:03:36.396 --> 01:03:37.397
Well, just say it.

01:03:38.898 --> 01:03:41.318
Why don't you say it? TEDDY:
Nah, you should just say it.

01:03:41.443 --> 01:03:43.236
(TEDDY CHUCKLES)
MICHELLE: You go ahead.

01:03:43.320 --> 01:03:44.321
TEDDY:
No, I insist.

01:03:44.404 --> 01:03:47.157
MICHELLE: No,
please. After you.

01:03:48.908 --> 01:03:50.869
Colony Collapse Disorder.

01:03:57.709 --> 01:03:59.294
Sure, Teddy. Like CCD.

01:04:00.170 --> 01:04:02.380
You're a bit of
an expert on CCD.

01:04:02.464 --> 01:04:05.091
MICHELLE: Well, I...
lwouldn't say that exactly.

01:04:05.175 --> 01:04:07.385
Well, I would
say that exactly.

01:04:08.887 --> 01:04:10.388
It's all right.
We're just talking.

01:04:11.723 --> 01:04:14.642
So, I take it you're referring
to the neonicotinoids

01:04:14.726 --> 01:04:16.144
that my
company makes.

01:04:17.187 --> 01:04:18.855
You know what? Let's
just... Let's just leave it.

01:04:18.938 --> 01:04:21.024
No, I-- I appreciate
your concern.

01:04:21.775 --> 01:04:24.694
I just think your research
is a bit out of date, Teddy.

01:04:25.612 --> 01:04:28.156
Uh, CCD has declined
significantly in recent years.

01:04:28.239 --> 01:04:29.824
The bees are
coming back.

01:04:30.658 --> 01:04:31.993
And there's
no consensus

01:04:32.077 --> 01:04:34.496
that pesticides were ever
a real threat to begin with.

01:04:36.247 --> 01:04:39.709
Yes, I'm well aware of what
you've all been telling us.

01:04:40.543 --> 01:04:41.544
Thank you.

01:04:43.004 --> 01:04:46.508
I know you want there to
be a master plan, Teddy.

01:04:47.801 --> 01:04:51.930
You want the bees to be dying
so that it can be my fault

01:04:52.847 --> 01:04:54.557
and you don't have to think
about the real reasons

01:04:54.641 --> 01:04:55.892
why species die.

01:04:57.060 --> 01:05:00.522
Immunodeficiencies,
changing habitats,

01:05:00.605 --> 01:05:01.898
genetic factors.

01:05:03.525 --> 01:05:05.902
Or sometimes a species
just winds down.

01:05:05.985 --> 01:05:07.404
(SCOFFS)

01:05:07.487 --> 01:05:08.947
"Winds down"?

01:05:09.697 --> 01:05:11.825
Maybe something clicks
in their heads.

01:05:11.908 --> 01:05:12.909
And they just know.

01:05:13.827 --> 01:05:15.161
Or they intuit.

01:05:16.079 --> 01:05:18.832
The futility of
the entire enterprise.

01:05:20.917 --> 01:05:22.544
Who knows, right?

01:05:23.378 --> 01:05:25.046
Right. Who knows?

01:05:25.130 --> 01:05:28.174
MICHELLE: That's right.
So hard to say.

01:05:28.258 --> 01:05:29.259
(TEDDY GASPS)

01:05:29.342 --> 01:05:30.343
Who knows, Don?

01:05:35.181 --> 01:05:37.016
We were having
a nice dinner.

01:05:37.100 --> 01:05:38.268
We were.

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:41.771
TEDDY: Nice,
quiet, respectful.

01:05:43.189 --> 01:05:44.190
But now we're not.

01:05:45.108 --> 01:05:46.109
No, we're not.

01:05:46.192 --> 01:05:48.528
TEDDY: And why do
you suppose that is?

01:05:50.738 --> 01:05:51.739
MICHELLE:
You tell me.

01:05:52.490 --> 01:05:53.700
Because you're
lying to me.

01:05:53.783 --> 01:05:55.368
Are you sure I
can't use the bathr--

01:05:55.452 --> 01:05:56.453
Shh!

01:05:57.787 --> 01:05:59.122
MICHELLE: Your
usual conclusion.

01:06:00.874 --> 01:06:02.459
TEDDY: You're
murdering the bees.

01:06:03.209 --> 01:06:04.210
I am not.

01:06:04.294 --> 01:06:06.379
TEDDY: And now
you're lying again.

01:06:07.380 --> 01:06:08.590
Lies.
Lies.

01:06:08.673 --> 01:06:10.675
Truth.
TEDDY: Lies.

01:06:10.758 --> 01:06:12.051
What's the
difference?

01:06:13.595 --> 01:06:14.596
I can't change
your mind.

01:06:14.679 --> 01:06:16.306
TEDDY: You're right.
You can't.

01:06:16.389 --> 01:06:19.267
Because I know
who you are.

01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:21.102
I know what you are.

01:06:23.104 --> 01:06:25.440
I know you
too, Teddy.

01:06:27.192 --> 01:06:28.359
Bullshit you do.

01:06:29.319 --> 01:06:30.320
MICHELLE; I do.

01:06:31.654 --> 01:06:32.655
You know
how I know?

01:06:33.281 --> 01:06:34.324
Fuck you.

01:06:36.618 --> 01:06:37.619
Sandy Gatz.

01:06:41.623 --> 01:06:42.624
What did you say?

01:06:45.084 --> 01:06:46.085
MICHELLE:
I remember, Teddy.

01:06:48.546 --> 01:06:50.381
That was your
mother. Right?

01:06:53.051 --> 01:06:54.260
She is my mother.

01:06:54.344 --> 01:06:55.595
MICHELLE: Right,
yes. Of course.

01:06:55.678 --> 01:06:57.013
(CLEARS THROAT)
I'm sorry.

01:06:58.306 --> 01:07:00.475
And you will never
say her name again.

01:07:00.558 --> 01:07:01.559
Understand?

01:07:02.393 --> 01:07:03.478
MICHELLE: That's
fair enough.

01:07:04.646 --> 01:07:06.814
But I do think
we need to discuss...

01:07:06.898 --> 01:07:08.525
TEDDY: We
actually do not.

01:07:08.608 --> 01:07:10.610
Because this
is not about that.

01:07:10.693 --> 01:07:12.445
MICHELLE: With all
due respect, Teddy,

01:07:12.529 --> 01:07:14.697
how could this
not be about that?

01:07:14.781 --> 01:07:16.824
We believed we
were helping, Teddy.

01:07:16.908 --> 01:07:18.451
Don't you dare.

01:07:18.535 --> 01:07:21.496
MICHELLE: (STAMMERS) Opioid
withdrawal medication like that

01:07:21.579 --> 01:07:22.872
could've helped
your mother

01:07:22.997 --> 01:07:25.291
and millions like
her. Stop. Just stop.

01:07:25.375 --> 01:07:27.001
MICHELLE: And the clinical
trial pay,

01:07:27.085 --> 01:07:28.545
that was
helping her, too.

01:07:28.628 --> 01:07:31.047
I know it wasn't a
king's ransom, but it...

01:07:31.130 --> 01:07:32.799
TEDDY: Stop right now.

01:07:32.882 --> 01:07:36.219
Obviously, we did not
foresee the complications,

01:07:36.302 --> 01:07:37.804
for Sandy or
for the others.

01:07:37.887 --> 01:07:39.013
Do not say her name.

01:07:39.097 --> 01:07:40.974
You do not say her name.

01:07:41.057 --> 01:07:43.518
We believed we paid your
family a proper reparation,

01:07:43.601 --> 01:07:45.853
but now I see
it wasn't nearly enough.

01:07:45.937 --> 01:07:47.355
TEDDY: Stop!
Not by half,

01:07:47.438 --> 01:07:48.648
not by a fraction.

01:07:48.731 --> 01:07:50.024
Stop!
MICHELLE: Teddy...

01:07:50.108 --> 01:07:51.859
you're right to
distrust me, you are.

01:07:51.985 --> 01:07:54.362
I lost myself somewhere,
okay? TEDDY: Fuck you.

01:07:54.445 --> 01:07:55.947
Shut the fuck up.
MICHELLE: I...

01:07:56.030 --> 01:07:58.157
I became a human being

01:07:58.241 --> 01:07:59.576
that I told myself
I would never become.

01:07:59.659 --> 01:08:01.494
Fuck you! MICHELLE:
I'm not denying that,

01:08:01.578 --> 01:08:03.037
but I can
help you, Teddy.

01:08:03.121 --> 01:08:04.706
I can still
help you.

01:08:04.789 --> 01:08:06.541
And I can still help
your mother.

01:08:06.624 --> 01:08:08.251
I can help her.

01:08:08.334 --> 01:08:09.544
Truly, I can.

01:08:09.627 --> 01:08:11.671
DON: I-- I...
I mean,

01:08:11.754 --> 01:08:12.755
can you?

01:08:15.091 --> 01:08:16.092
You needed a mother.

01:08:17.510 --> 01:08:18.553
She was never
there for you.

01:08:18.636 --> 01:08:19.762
Fucking die,
you fucker!

01:08:19.846 --> 01:08:22.390
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

01:08:22.473 --> 01:08:25.184
(MICHELLE GRUNTING)

01:08:25.268 --> 01:08:26.853
TEDDY: Fucking
kill you!

01:08:26.936 --> 01:08:28.563
I'll fucking
kill you!

01:08:33.109 --> 01:08:34.902
Teddy, stop.

01:08:34.986 --> 01:08:36.988
(STRAINED GRUNTING)

01:08:41.951 --> 01:08:42.952
DON: Teddy, stop.

01:08:49.042 --> 01:08:50.043
(TEDDY CRIES OUT)

01:08:50.126 --> 01:08:51.127
(MICHELLE GASPING)

01:09:18.655 --> 01:09:20.657
(MUSIC FADES)

01:09:21.866 --> 01:09:24.410
(MICHELLE GRUNTING
IN OTHER ROOM)

01:09:27.205 --> 01:09:28.414
(MICHELLE GRUNTING)

01:09:30.750 --> 01:09:32.752
(MUSIC RESUMES)

01:09:36.297 --> 01:09:37.298
(MICHELLE YELLS)

01:09:39.509 --> 01:09:40.802
Get Off him!

01:09:40.885 --> 01:09:41.886
You can't beat me.

01:09:41.969 --> 01:09:44.138
Because you are a loser
and I am a winner.

01:09:44.222 --> 01:09:45.640
And that's
fucking life.

01:09:49.769 --> 01:09:50.770
(THUDS)

01:09:50.853 --> 01:09:53.147
(TEDDY BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:09:55.233 --> 01:09:56.234
(DOORBELL RINGS)

01:10:09.080 --> 01:10:10.081
(KNOCKING SOFTLY)

01:10:19.924 --> 01:10:21.926
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

01:10:53.082 --> 01:10:54.751
TEDDY: Hey.
Hey.

01:10:54.834 --> 01:10:55.835
How annoying
is this, right?

01:10:55.918 --> 01:10:57.837
TEDDY: No, what's up?
Mmm.

01:10:57.920 --> 01:10:58.921
No, come on,
dude. I know.

01:10:59.005 --> 01:11:00.339
It's like, "Why'd I
even tell this guy

01:11:00.423 --> 01:11:02.258
"he could stop by,"
right? (CHUCKLES)

01:11:02.341 --> 01:11:03.885
TEDDY: It's fine,
Casey. What's up?

01:11:03.968 --> 01:11:05.344
Um, sorry.

01:11:05.428 --> 01:11:07.346
I-- I actually do have a real
reason to be here, though.

01:11:08.139 --> 01:11:09.140
TEDDY: Uh-huh.

01:11:09.223 --> 01:11:11.142
Um, well, you know how
we're all working

01:11:11.225 --> 01:11:12.393
this missing
persons thing?

01:11:15.021 --> 01:11:16.022
Uh, yeah,

01:11:16.105 --> 01:11:18.024
I just had a couple questions
to run by you, actually.

01:11:19.317 --> 01:11:20.359
Don't worry.

01:11:20.443 --> 01:11:22.528
Obviously, I just, um...

01:11:22.612 --> 01:11:25.281
Sorry, could I actually
come in, maybe?

01:11:26.699 --> 01:11:27.700
TEDDY: Uh, yeah.
No, sure.

01:11:27.784 --> 01:11:28.910
Come on in.

01:11:28.993 --> 01:11:30.661
CASEY: Dude, thank you.
I really appreciate that.

01:11:36.459 --> 01:11:37.460
(DOOR CLOSES)

01:11:38.503 --> 01:11:40.004
"We are not alone."

01:11:40.087 --> 01:11:41.130
TEDDY; Huh?

01:11:41.214 --> 01:11:43.424
Nothing.
Just, you know,

01:11:43.508 --> 01:11:45.092
"We are not alone."

01:11:45.176 --> 01:11:46.427
TEDDY: Oh, right.

01:11:46.511 --> 01:11:48.054
Well, we're not.

01:11:48.179 --> 01:11:49.472
Uh... CASEY: Right.

01:11:49.931 --> 01:11:51.432
TEDDY: You want
some water or...

01:11:51.516 --> 01:11:53.100
CASEY: That'd be great.
Thank you.

01:11:54.018 --> 01:11:55.269
(CASEY SIGHS)

01:11:55.353 --> 01:11:56.646
Gotta tell you,
man, it's, uh,

01:11:57.939 --> 01:11:59.649
pretty weird
being back in here.

01:12:01.025 --> 01:12:02.235
A lot of feelings.

01:12:07.365 --> 01:12:09.784
Yeah, well,
same old shit.

01:12:09.867 --> 01:12:10.910
CASEY: Hmm.

01:12:10.993 --> 01:12:11.994
Thank you.

01:12:12.995 --> 01:12:15.039
Scared the, uh,
chair's gonna run away?

01:12:15.915 --> 01:12:16.916
TEDDY: What?

01:12:20.586 --> 01:12:22.588
Oh. No.

01:12:22.672 --> 01:12:25.508
My mom, she used to have
fits or whatever,

01:12:25.591 --> 01:12:27.343
so we'd... we'd nail
the chair down.

01:12:29.136 --> 01:12:30.137
Yeah.

01:12:32.473 --> 01:12:33.766
(CHUCKLES) Uh-oh.

01:12:33.850 --> 01:12:34.851
What?

01:12:35.768 --> 01:12:36.769
My archnemesis.

01:12:39.814 --> 01:12:41.023
TEDDY: Ah.

01:12:41.691 --> 01:12:43.317
You want a
piece of cake?

01:12:43.943 --> 01:12:45.528
I mean,
if you insist.

01:12:45.611 --> 01:12:47.321
(CASEY LAUGHS)

01:12:47.405 --> 01:12:48.489
Yeah, I love
this stuff.

01:12:50.157 --> 01:12:51.158
(CUTLERY CLATTERING)

01:12:56.163 --> 01:12:58.541
So, um, you had
some questions or...

01:12:58.624 --> 01:13:00.835
Oh. Uh,
yes, sorry.

01:13:00.918 --> 01:13:02.545
Um, you're still
atAuxolith, right?

01:13:02.628 --> 01:13:03.921
Yeah.

01:13:04.005 --> 01:13:05.882
So you must know all
about the Fuller case?

01:13:06.883 --> 01:13:09.176
I mean, I heard
a little, yeah.

01:13:09.260 --> 01:13:10.928
On the news?

01:13:11.012 --> 01:13:13.055
I don't get the news
from the news.

01:13:13.139 --> 01:13:14.765
CASEY: Right. Um,
of course. Sorry.

01:13:14.849 --> 01:13:16.142
I'm just here
on a hunch, really.

01:13:16.225 --> 01:13:17.977
See, this missing
lady, her phone

01:13:18.060 --> 01:13:20.229
pinged a cell tower in the
area the night of the abduction.

01:13:20.313 --> 01:13:21.564
Thank you.
Thank you very much.

01:13:21.647 --> 01:13:22.899
TEDDY: Oh.

01:13:23.733 --> 01:13:26.152
Well, those things have
a pretty wide radius,

01:13:26.277 --> 01:13:28.070
though, right? CASEY:
Yeah, no, for sure.

01:13:28.154 --> 01:13:31.073
It's just that her car was
also snapped by a speed trap

01:13:31.157 --> 01:13:33.701
near the intersection
down the road over here.

01:13:33.784 --> 01:13:34.785
TEDDY: Oh, yeah?

01:13:36.287 --> 01:13:37.955
I know. I'm, uh...

01:13:38.039 --> 01:13:39.415
You know,
long shot, right?

01:13:39.498 --> 01:13:41.876
But, I don't know, it's a
sparsely populated area.

01:13:41.959 --> 01:13:43.794
Figured I'd check in
with the local residents.

01:13:43.878 --> 01:13:45.296
See if, uh,

01:13:45.379 --> 01:13:47.590
you or Don seen
anything peculiar.

01:13:48.841 --> 01:13:49.842
Uh...

01:13:51.010 --> 01:13:52.637
No, no.

01:13:52.720 --> 01:13:53.721
CASEY: Well,
uh, hmm.

01:13:53.804 --> 01:13:55.598
Let's see here.

01:13:55.681 --> 01:13:58.809
For starters,
have you seen...

01:14:00.645 --> 01:14:02.188
this car?

01:14:03.230 --> 01:14:04.440
TEDDY: Uh-uh.

01:14:05.316 --> 01:14:08.194
What about, uh,
this woman?

01:14:09.570 --> 01:14:12.073
I mean, yeah, she--
She owns my work, yeah.

01:14:12.156 --> 01:14:13.616
But I haven't
seen her, no.

01:14:13.699 --> 01:14:15.076
You haven't seen
her in person?

01:14:15.159 --> 01:14:16.160
No.

01:14:16.285 --> 01:14:19.205
I scan packages, so I
wouldn't. (CHUCKLES)

01:14:19.288 --> 01:14:21.123
No,no.Dude, I-- I
know. I'm-- I'm sorry.

01:14:21.207 --> 01:14:23.000
Um, how about
your neighbors?

01:14:23.084 --> 01:14:24.877
They say anything
about, I don't know,

01:14:24.961 --> 01:14:27.713
any out of the
ordinary activity?

01:14:27.797 --> 01:14:30.341
Uh, I mean, I don't
know them, really.

01:14:31.550 --> 01:14:33.177
Right. I--
I'm sorry, man.

01:14:33.260 --> 01:14:35.721
Uh, I'm really
grasping at straws here.

01:14:38.140 --> 01:14:39.141
Uh...

01:14:39.976 --> 01:14:42.979
Look, I mainly just wanted
to check up on you, man.

01:14:43.729 --> 01:14:44.772
I know the last
thing you want

01:14:44.855 --> 01:14:47.942
is for your fucked-up
babysitter from 20 years ago

01:14:48.025 --> 01:14:50.778
stopping by, feeling
guilty about, um...

01:14:52.279 --> 01:14:55.199
you know, whatever
went down, uh, but...

01:14:56.534 --> 01:14:57.576
Sometimes I pass
by this place,

01:14:57.660 --> 01:15:02.456
and I just get this fucking
sad, awful feeling, like,

01:15:03.416 --> 01:15:04.750
"What's going
on in there?"

01:15:06.752 --> 01:15:08.045
You know?

01:15:08.129 --> 01:15:09.672
Not much.
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

01:15:09.755 --> 01:15:10.756
(GROANS)

01:15:13.551 --> 01:15:14.552
(SIGHS)

01:15:21.183 --> 01:15:22.184
Where is he?

01:15:22.268 --> 01:15:24.270
(CHAINS RATTLING)

01:15:33.654 --> 01:15:35.656
Don? Look
at me, Don.

01:15:37.450 --> 01:15:39.118
Put the gun down.
Look at me.

01:15:40.411 --> 01:15:41.787
I know you would
never hurt me.

01:15:45.082 --> 01:15:46.083
(PAINED GRUNTING)

01:15:48.461 --> 01:15:50.546
(CHAIN RATTLING)

01:15:57.136 --> 01:15:58.471
Thank you, Don.

01:16:00.431 --> 01:16:03.601
You could've shot me
earlier upstairs, but you didn't.

01:16:07.313 --> 01:16:09.607
How you behaved
was honestly heroic.

01:16:12.193 --> 01:16:13.569
I don't use
that word lightly.

01:16:15.654 --> 01:16:17.573
You have been the only
thing stopping him

01:16:17.656 --> 01:16:20.367
from doing
God-knows-what to me.

01:16:21.035 --> 01:16:22.536
I don't
talk to you.

01:16:24.330 --> 01:16:26.082
That's how it is.

01:16:27.166 --> 01:16:28.584
So stay quiet.

01:16:29.251 --> 01:16:30.836
But you know
this is crazy, right?

01:16:33.005 --> 01:16:35.007
You know this is wrong.

01:16:35.382 --> 01:16:36.759
I know you
know that.

01:16:36.842 --> 01:16:37.843
Shut up.

01:16:37.927 --> 01:16:38.928
MICHELLE: I'm
just saying.

01:16:40.012 --> 01:16:41.013
There's a
world, Don.

01:16:42.014 --> 01:16:44.642
There is a world
where we help you

01:16:44.725 --> 01:16:47.103
and your cousin
and your aunt,

01:16:47.186 --> 01:16:50.731
where reparations are paid
and a page is turned.

01:16:51.899 --> 01:16:53.734
All of that can
happen for you.

01:16:53.818 --> 01:16:55.361
No. You're...

01:16:56.278 --> 01:16:58.280
You're gonna get
me and Teddy arrested.

01:16:58.364 --> 01:16:59.865
MICHELLE:
No, I wouldn't.

01:16:59.949 --> 01:17:01.200
And if
you're right

01:17:01.283 --> 01:17:02.576
and Teddy
gets arrested,

01:17:02.660 --> 01:17:06.163
it'll all be different
for you, Don.

01:17:06.789 --> 01:17:09.250
It will, if you
let me go.

01:17:09.333 --> 01:17:10.626
Stop.

01:17:10.709 --> 01:17:11.919
I know what
you're doing.

01:17:14.630 --> 01:17:19.844
All he does is drag you
deeper and deeper into a pit.

01:17:21.178 --> 01:17:24.473
He never actually offers
you a way out for you.

01:17:24.557 --> 01:17:25.558
(DON GRUNTS)

01:17:25.641 --> 01:17:27.768
I can do that for you, Don.

01:17:29.103 --> 01:17:30.479
I want to do that for you.

01:17:30.563 --> 01:17:33.232
I said, shut up!

01:17:33.315 --> 01:17:34.692
MICHELLE:
It's okay.

01:17:34.775 --> 01:17:37.486
I know you're confused
and frustrated.

01:17:37.570 --> 01:17:41.490
No one in the universe
could possibly blame you.

01:17:41.574 --> 01:17:42.741
Shut up.

01:17:43.826 --> 01:17:44.994
MICHELLE:
Put the gun down.

01:17:45.744 --> 01:17:46.871
Just talk to me.

01:17:46.954 --> 01:17:48.247
DON: No.
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

01:17:48.330 --> 01:17:49.999
Sit down and talk to me.
Put the gun down.

01:17:50.082 --> 01:17:51.959
Just shut up,

01:17:52.042 --> 01:17:53.878
alien filth.

01:17:55.546 --> 01:17:56.672
CASEY: He
ever show up again?

01:18:00.968 --> 01:18:01.969
Fucking asshole.

01:18:03.179 --> 01:18:05.181
Sorry. I know he's your dad
and you probably love him.

01:18:06.390 --> 01:18:08.601
I literally wouldn't
recognize him.

01:18:12.521 --> 01:18:14.857
CASEY: (SIGHS HEAVILY)
Look, Teddy, um...

01:18:16.317 --> 01:18:18.068
I know it was a
long time ago,

01:18:18.152 --> 01:18:19.361
what I did to you, man.

01:18:20.487 --> 01:18:21.488
It's fine.

01:18:21.572 --> 01:18:23.199
CASEY: No.
It wasn't fine.

01:18:23.282 --> 01:18:26.160
It-- it was wrong,
but I promise you,

01:18:26.243 --> 01:18:27.244
it's-- It's not
'cause I liked it.

01:18:27.328 --> 01:18:28.370
It was just...

01:18:28.454 --> 01:18:29.747
you know, probably
some weird power thing.

01:18:29.830 --> 01:18:33.083
I was... I was young
and lost, and...

01:18:33.167 --> 01:18:34.627
I promise you, dude,

01:18:34.710 --> 01:18:37.379
I never, ever did
that to anybody else.

01:18:38.172 --> 01:18:39.757
Just forget it.
It's done.

01:18:40.174 --> 01:18:41.175
Seriously.

01:18:42.009 --> 01:18:43.219
Really?
TEDDY: Mmm-hmm.

01:18:44.094 --> 01:18:46.013
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

01:18:48.682 --> 01:18:49.683
Hey, you
should read this.

01:18:50.392 --> 01:18:51.435
This shit helped
me a lot.

01:18:53.938 --> 01:18:54.939
Thank you,
dude.

01:18:56.398 --> 01:18:57.524
Hey, you want
to see my bees?

01:19:00.694 --> 01:19:01.779
MICHELLE: Someone's
up there, right?

01:19:03.322 --> 01:19:05.241
Um... Shut up.

01:19:06.617 --> 01:19:07.618
Is it the police?

01:19:08.077 --> 01:19:09.745
I said, shut up.

01:19:10.329 --> 01:19:11.330
MICHELLE: It is.

01:19:11.789 --> 01:19:13.916
And, Don, they're gonna
arrest your cousin.

01:19:14.750 --> 01:19:16.752
But it is not
too late for you.

01:19:17.294 --> 01:19:19.421
Please, stop.

01:19:20.130 --> 01:19:21.590
If you let me
go right now,

01:19:22.758 --> 01:19:24.551
everything will work
out for you.

01:19:24.635 --> 01:19:25.928
No, it won't.

01:19:26.011 --> 01:19:27.554
MICHELLE:
It Will, Don.

01:19:29.473 --> 01:19:30.474
I promise.

01:19:30.933 --> 01:19:32.351
You don't understand.

01:19:32.434 --> 01:19:34.228
There's nothing
left for me.

01:19:35.104 --> 01:19:36.647
Teddy is all I have.

01:19:38.148 --> 01:19:40.359
We'll find something
else for you.

01:19:41.610 --> 01:19:42.611
You don't need him.

01:19:42.695 --> 01:19:44.029
Yes, I do.

01:19:45.239 --> 01:19:46.365
I love him.

01:19:48.784 --> 01:19:50.452
TEDDY: Sorry I couldn't
help you find that lady.

01:19:50.536 --> 01:19:51.537
CASEY: It's
all right, man.

01:19:51.620 --> 01:19:53.622
(BEES BUZZING QUIETLY)

01:20:00.212 --> 01:20:01.213
CASEY:
I got it.

01:20:01.297 --> 01:20:02.548
TEDDY: Thanks.

01:20:02.631 --> 01:20:05.009
Be gentle. Yep, yep- (GRUNTS)

01:20:11.307 --> 01:20:15.144
There is so much else
out there, Don.

01:20:15.686 --> 01:20:16.687
No, there's not.

01:20:17.438 --> 01:20:18.439
Not here.

01:20:19.023 --> 01:20:20.024
MICHELLE:
Then where?

01:20:20.691 --> 01:20:21.817
Where do you
want to go, Don?

01:20:23.277 --> 01:20:24.278
We can go there.

01:20:24.653 --> 01:20:25.654
I'll take you there.

01:20:27.031 --> 01:20:28.949
If you are an alien,

01:20:29.033 --> 01:20:30.284
will you help me?

01:20:30.367 --> 01:20:33.787
Don, that's enough
of that. Please.

01:20:33.871 --> 01:20:36.457
You know I'm not an alien.
You know that.

01:20:37.166 --> 01:20:38.334
But if you are,

01:20:39.043 --> 01:20:40.627
would you take
me with you?

01:20:43.005 --> 01:20:44.006
What?

01:20:44.089 --> 01:20:45.799
DON: If all of
this is true

01:20:45.883 --> 01:20:48.427
and you have
a sh-- spaceship,

01:20:49.845 --> 01:20:51.513
would you take me
away from here?

01:20:56.060 --> 01:20:57.061
Of course, Don.

01:20:58.145 --> 01:20:59.521
Yes, absolutely.

01:21:00.606 --> 01:21:01.690
I'll take you
with me.

01:21:03.442 --> 01:21:04.443
We'll leave Earth.

01:21:06.403 --> 01:21:08.405
I promise that's
what'll happen, okay?

01:21:10.449 --> 01:21:11.700
If you let me go.

01:21:15.621 --> 01:21:16.622
Thank you...

01:21:17.790 --> 01:21:19.708
but not without Teddy.

01:21:19.792 --> 01:21:22.044
MICHELLE: Please, Don,
we don't have much time.

01:21:22.127 --> 01:21:24.171
Th-- They're gonna
break in here at any minute,

01:21:24.254 --> 01:21:25.756
and then I won't
be able to help you.

01:21:27.049 --> 01:21:28.050
(DON GRUNTS SOFTLY)

01:21:30.094 --> 01:21:31.095
Come on.

01:21:41.271 --> 01:21:42.940
(TAKES DEEP BREATH)

01:21:44.900 --> 01:21:45.901
Okay.

01:21:46.318 --> 01:21:48.195
I'm ready to leave.

01:21:49.530 --> 01:21:50.531
Okay.

01:21:51.407 --> 01:21:53.117
DON: Can you do
one thing for me?

01:21:55.369 --> 01:21:58.747
Tell Teddy
that I'm sorry

01:21:58.831 --> 01:22:00.290
and that I love him.

01:22:02.543 --> 01:22:03.544
I will.

01:22:09.758 --> 01:22:10.759
(YELPS)

01:22:10.843 --> 01:22:13.011
(GUNSHOT IN DISTANCE)
CASEY: The fuck?

01:22:13.095 --> 01:22:14.513
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

01:22:17.808 --> 01:22:20.436
Jesus fucking Christ.

01:22:21.854 --> 01:22:24.106
(GRUNTING) Fuck.

01:22:24.189 --> 01:22:26.358
(BEES BUZZING)

01:22:26.442 --> 01:22:28.527
(PANICKED GRUNTING)

01:22:34.992 --> 01:22:36.994
(THUMPING)

01:22:44.042 --> 01:22:45.961
(THUMPING CONTINUES)

01:22:47.171 --> 01:22:49.173
(LIQUID SQUELCHING)

01:22:50.466 --> 01:22:52.509
(RUNNING FOOTSTEPS)
(GATE OPENS)

01:22:52.593 --> 01:22:54.094
TEDDY: Don?
(GATE CLOSES)

01:22:54.178 --> 01:22:55.179
Don!

01:22:58.056 --> 01:22:59.057
Jesus!

01:22:59.933 --> 01:23:00.934
Don.

01:23:01.018 --> 01:23:02.644
No, no, no, no, no, no.

01:23:02.728 --> 01:23:03.854
I swear to you,
he did it to himself.

01:23:03.937 --> 01:23:05.981
He thought the police were
coming... TEDDY: Don. No, no, no.

01:23:06.064 --> 01:23:07.399
...and he panicked,
and he just freaked out.

01:23:07.483 --> 01:23:08.484
Teddy, no. No.

01:23:08.567 --> 01:23:10.068
What did you say
to him? Nothing.

01:23:10.152 --> 01:23:11.862
(TEDDY PANTING)

01:23:11.945 --> 01:23:15.240
What fucking filth did
you fill his sad brain with,

01:23:15.324 --> 01:23:16.325
you demon
from hell?

01:23:16.408 --> 01:23:18.494
He was under
extreme pressure, Teddy.

01:23:18.577 --> 01:23:20.829
He cracked. TEDDY:
And you cracked him!

01:23:20.913 --> 01:23:23.290
You poisoned his heart
with lies and bullshit

01:23:23.373 --> 01:23:26.001
until his whole fucking world
collapsed, didn't you?

01:23:26.084 --> 01:23:27.961
You fed him a
fucking fairy tale.

01:23:28.045 --> 01:23:29.880
He did all of this for you,
you fucking maniac.

01:23:30.005 --> 01:23:31.548
Don't kill me, Teddy. (STAMMERS)

01:23:31.632 --> 01:23:34.009
I have a cure
for your mother.

01:23:36.220 --> 01:23:37.429
What? MICHELLE: There's a cure.

01:23:37.930 --> 01:23:39.181
You can save her.

01:23:41.642 --> 01:23:42.643
What are you saying?

01:23:42.726 --> 01:23:44.102
Inside of her,

01:23:45.270 --> 01:23:46.772
a big change
is taking place.

01:23:47.648 --> 01:23:49.608
It's an entire
rearranging

01:23:49.691 --> 01:23:51.985
